    phase "design-system" state="complete" worked-by="agent:principal-engineer" {
        approach "`continues` is a field on the iteration, referencing a prior iteration" {
            over "a `continuation` entity of its own, holding both iterations' ids"
            over "inferring it from `on-slice` overlap, with nothing written down"
            because "the same distinction `declare-an-entity-kind` already draws: a fact ABOUT \
                an iteration is a field, and only a thing the iteration CONTAINS needs `holds`. \
                A continuation is the first, and the field carries `references=\"iteration\"` for \
                free — the same generic reference check every other cross-reference gets"
        }

        approach "a carried claim is identified by a `carried-from` CITATION, never by the word `carried`" {
            over "reserving the literal state value `carried` for this feature"
            over "a boolean flag beside `state`, e.g. `inherited=#true`"
            because "the corpus already used `state=\"carried\"` as free prose for a claim a \
                FINDING carries forward (`ITER.260823.07`'s close accounting) — a fact this \
                design did not know until an existing close-accounting test broke on the first \
                build. Reusing the \
                word for a second, incompatible meaning would make the two indistinguishable by \
                the very engine meant to keep facts apart. The citation is the new fact; the word \
                stays free text either way, which is honest about how little of `claim` this \
                engine actually validates"
            note "carried, not settled: see F1"
        }

        approach "produced approaches are the union of a design's own and the one it continues" {
            over "requiring a continuing iteration to restate the approach in its own words"
            over "exempting a continuation from `implement-follows-an-approach` entirely"
            because "F2 of `ITER.260823.08` passed by holding NO design at all, which is the \
                right outcome — the claim was carried out — reached by a route that would have \
                looked identical for an iteration that carried out nothing. Naming the approach \
                it continues is the difference, so `produced` has to include it for `followed` \
                to ever resolve"
        }

        approach "an approach's disposition is graded on whether ITS OWN implement is complete" {
            over "always refusing an untaken approach, and exempting continuations from it"
            over "a new phase state meaning `in progress`, beside pending/active/complete/skipped"
            because "F4 of `ITER.260823.06` found the rule refusing the ordinary state of any \
                iteration that designed before it built. The phase already declares the state \
                that answers this — `active` and `pending` both mean not finished — so the fix \
                reads a fact the schema already carries rather than adding a fact to carry"
        }

        produced "four approaches, three new fields on `iteration`, two new rules and their \
            witnesses, and a severity split on a rule that already existed"
