    finding "F1" \
        text="the design's second approach exists because the FIRST attempt at it did not know \
            the corpus already spends the word `carried` on a claim a finding carries forward — \
            found only when an existing close-accounting test broke against the first build, not \
            by reasoning about the vocabulary beforehand. The word itself is still unreserved: \
            `claim` declares no field and nothing stops a third meaning being written under it. \
            Formalizing `claim` as a shaped, contained entity — the way `phase` was declared by \
            `ITER.260821.01` — would let a `one-of` catch this the way it now catches `phase` and \
            `iteration` themselves" \
        note="not owed against this slice: `TS.260823.10` explicitly excludes deciding what a \
            claim's own shape should be, and inventing that scope here would be exactly the \
            second-guessing `plan-before-building` asks an iteration not to do"
